Subject: [PATCH] R80b, part 3, patch 12 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M14;
 Review 80, the SM seat's finding 27, checked by main by a search): THE OLD
 SIGN OF THE INDEX FOR A UNIT ON ONE LINE IS CORRECTED WHERE IT STILL STOOD,
 AND B1894'S LOCK LOOKS FOR IT IN ITS OTHER WORDINGS.

THE STATEMENT IS MAIN'S, from the law map's row for B1641 as corrected on 2026-11-12: with units on the cusp's three lines, the Euler characteristic of the triplet's forms is their sum above its value at no unit, and the four-dimensional index takes that term with a minus sign; so at an empty Lambda+ the index is -3 for the uniform unit and -1 for a unit on one line. "A unit on one line gives one" is the dimension B1796 computed.

WHERE THE OLD SIGN STOOD, each with a dated correction beside it now, the old words kept: the changelog's entry of 2026-11-11; harvest row 1709; the law map's currency read of 2026-11-12; main's fourth message to the session whose finding it was, as a note at its head; the docstring of B1641's lock, which calls the Euler characteristic the index. The test's name stays, so that the test does not leave its lock.

B1894'S LOCK looked for the old sentence in one exact wording and saw none of these. A new test looks for two more wordings and asks that the sign stand within 700 characters after them, or at the head of the message that holds them. THE PLANTED CASES, in the test: each of the four pages as it stood, its correction taken out; each is reported, and the older test passes on all four.

LEFT AS IT IS, and said: the heading of B1641's dated note of 2026-11-11 says that a unit on one line gives one. Under it the note's second correction says that the bullets write "the index" for two different things. The changelog's sentence is also corrected in a new entry, in this part's last patch. All 53 gates pass. 0 of 19.
